# Auto commit with change details

When a task changes files, commit that work before you stop. Do not wait to be asked again.

## When to commit

- Commit once the task is done and the related files are saved.
- One task, one commit. Keep unrelated edits out of the same commit.
- Skip secrets (`.env`, credentials, tokens) and warn if they were requested.
- Do not create an empty commit.
- Do not push unless the user asks.

## Commit message

The message must say what changed and why. Name the files and the behavior that changed.

```
Add auto-commit rule for finished agent work.

- Add .cursor/rules/auto-commit.mdc so each finished change is committed.
- Require the message to list the files and the behavior that changed.
```

Use a short first line, a blank line, then bullets for the actual edits.
